    "summary": "SPF measures how much UVB radiation a sunscreen blocks, with SPF 30 blocking 97% and SPF 50 blocking 98% — making gains above SPF 50 marginal. For most people, a broad-spectrum SPF 30 applied generously and reapplied every two hours offers sufficient and practical sun protection.",
